"""
A receipt issued after the money has arrived.

This is NOT a VAT invoice: it has no tax code, no seller information, no digital signature, and
invoiceNumber is an internal code that does not belong to a serial range registered with the tax
authority. Do not build a UI that promises school accountants this is a deductible document.

It has only two fields, and that is everything the invoice knows by itself: the amount, what was
bought and how it was paid all live on Order and Payment. That is why it has no query of its own --
always read it through Order.invoice.
"""
type Invoice {
    "Unique across the whole system, in the form INV-{year}-{12 hex characters}. This is the code the school reads out to support when something needs to be looked up."
    invoiceNumber: String!
    "The year inside invoiceNumber is taken in Vietnam time, so it always matches the date shown here when this timestamp is read in Vietnam time."
    issueDate: DateTime!
}

# Declared with extend so that order.graphqls does not need to know about invoices: the relation is
# 1-1 and the invoice is the dependent side. Spring GraphQL merges every .graphqls file into one
# schema, so a type in another file can still be attached.
extend type Order {
    """
    NULL when the order has not collected any money yet, and that is the correct answer rather than
    missing data: only a SUCCESS order gets an invoice. Use the presence of this field to mark which
    rows in the history actually brought in money.
    """
    invoice: Invoice
}
